1657	194	bot	I’m sorry you’re feeling this way; it’s understandable to want some relief.  \n<ul>\n<li>Practice slow, deep breathing – inhale for 4 seconds, hold 2 seconds, exhale for 6 seconds.</li>\n<li>Identify early warning signs (e.g., rapid heartbeat, racing thoughts) and pause to use a grounding technique, such as naming five things you can see.</li>\n<li>Maintain regular sleep, meals, and gentle exercise to keep your body’s stress response balanced.</li>\n<li>Limit caffeine and alcohol, which can heighten anxiety.</li>\n<li>If panic attacks keep occurring, consider talking to the school counselor or a mental‑health professional for additional support.</li>\n</ul>\nRemember, these tips are for general wellness and not a substitute for professional care. If you ever feel unsafe or the panic becomes overwhelming, please seek immediate help at the clinic or call <a href="tel:+639076842769">0907-684-2769</a>.	sent	2026-09-01 00:01:32.568013+00
