1694	199	bot	Rabies usually starts with fever, headache, and a feeling of weakness or discomfort at the bite site, then can progress to confusion, agitation, difficulty swallowing, and fear of water (hydrophobia).<br><br>Common early and later signs include:<br><ul><li>Fever and chills</li><li>Headache or neck stiffness</li><li>Pain or tingling around the bite</li><li>Restlessness or irritability</li><li>Difficulty swallowing and fear of water</li></ul><br>These symptoms can become serious quickly. Please visit the clinic as soon as possible for a proper assessment, or call us at <a href="tel:+639076842769">0907-684-2769</a>. This information is for educational purposes only and not a medical diagnosis.	sent	2026-09-02 16:29:56.600131+00
